      "body": "## Motivation\n\nAdd CPU platform support for the Ling series of models.\n\n- `inclusionAI/Ling-3.0-flash`: Throws an error when `extra_buffer` is not set.\n- `inclusionAI/Ling-3.0-tiny`: Convolution weights bypass the `dtype` check, causing FP32 data to be passed into a packed kernel that only supports FP16/BF16.\n\n## Modifications\nThe following modifications have been made to address these issues:\n- `inclusionAI/Ling-3.0-flash`: Added a platform capability check before selecting `extra_buffer`; falls back to `no_buffer` if unsupported.\n- `inclusionAI/Ling-3.0-tiny`: For unsupported `dtype` values, the original weights are retained and AMX is disabled for that layer; low-precision weights continue to follow the existing execution path without forced precision conversion.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41400986150](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41400986150)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41400986136](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41400986136)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41400986014](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41400986014)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
